From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:50:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: debug mode: create the save folder, skipped movies end
 at their last frame

- Saving a state wrote debug-states.bin next to the save file without
  creating its folder; a game that has never saved (fresh STEINS;GATE 0
  install) has none, so the write failed and the state was lost at the next
  start. The folder is created first now.
- Skipping a movie (button or forced skip) stopped the player but left
  SW_MOVIEFRAME where it was. STEINS;GATE 0 waits for movies by polling that
  counter (MACROSYS2 label 310 waits for frame > 20 after the world line
  change movie), so the script looped forever. A skipped movie on channel 0
  now leaves the counter at its last frame (SW_MOVIETOTALFRAME - 1), as if it
  had ended.

Generic; can go upstream together with the debug mode.

Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device), sg0-pc
(Steam data, Chinese scripts): state saved at SG0_B01_06 #1516 and loaded from
the title after a restart; x64 forced skip passes the world line change movie
of SG0_B01_06 and goes on to SG0_B01_12. sg-pc: x64 forced skip through the
first world line change of SG00_01.

diff --git a/src/debugtools.cpp b/src/debugtools.cpp
index 0fad2029c923e3a0d3df51342034c7febce19ef8..9b22689c86bd0fecd8e6d28187ab35a47ad2510f 100644
--- a/src/debugtools.cpp
+++ b/src/debugtools.cpp
@@ -244,6 +244,9 @@ bool GetVector(std::ifstream& f, std::vector<T>& v) {
 constexpr uint32_t StatesMagic = 0x32534454;  // "TDS2"
 
 void WriteStates() {
+  // the save folder only exists once the game has saved; a fresh install has none yet
+  std::error_code ec;
+  std::filesystem::create_directories(std::filesystem::path(StatesPath()).parent_path(), ec);
   std::ofstream f(StatesPath(), std::ios::binary | std::ios::trunc);
   if (!f) {
     LastMessage = L("cannot write ", "无法写入 ") + StatesPath();
@@ -299,6 +302,8 @@ void SkipMovies(bool keepLooping = false) {
     const int mode = ScrWork[SW_MOVIE_PLAYMODE + 20 * i] % 20 % 8;
     if (keepLooping && (mode == 2 || mode == 3 || mode == 5)) continue;
     Video::Players[i]->Stop();
+    // STEINS;GATE 0 polls the frame counter (e.g. MACROSYS2 label 310 waits for frame 20)
+    if (i == 0) ScrWork[SW_MOVIEFRAME] = std::max(ScrWork[SW_MOVIETOTALFRAME] - 1, ScrWork[SW_MOVIEFRAME]);
     SetFlag(SF_MOVIEPLAY + i, false);
     SetFlag(SF_MOVIE_DRAWWAIT + i, false);  // scripts wait for the first frame before they wait for the end
   }
